{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Now why do you cry out a cry</b> — raise a shout and raise your voice like a <i>teru'ah</i>, as in: \"and Joshua heard the sound of the people in its crying out [ברעה]\" — and behold <b>the cry [הרע]</b> falls upon the answer of the mighty and upon the weak. Also this <b>you cry out a cry [תריעי ריע]</b> falls upon the language of outcry and weeping." "<b>Is there no king in you</b> — the meaning: why do you cry out as though you have no savior and counselor, and therefore he strengthened you like a woman in labor — is not HaShem your king and your counselor, who says to you: do not cry out. Rather, be in travail and give birth, from the language of \"for she travailed and also gave birth.\" Rather, if now you go forth and walk in exile and arrive as far as Babylon, there you will be delivered, there he will redeem you — your king and your counselor is HaShem."], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:14:02.539243479Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}